  <data name="FAQ1 Question" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>When is the deadline for initiative submission?</value>
  </data>
  <data name="FAQ1 Answer" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Usually, the University receives initiative applications in two periods per academic year. Period 1 in November and Period 2 in April.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="FAQ2 Question" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>How many authors can an initiative have?</value>
  </data>
  <data name="FAQ2 Answer" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>An initiative can be carried out by an individual or a group of authors (maximum 3 members).</value>
  </data>
  <data name="FAQ3 Question" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Can I edit my application after submission?</value>
  </data>
  <data name="FAQ3 Answer" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Lecturers can only edit applications when the status shows "Waiting for Modification" or before the Council begins evaluation.</value>
